Fillets: a stripe cut to nothing between its corners leaves its curve to
a periodic corner surface in that surface's own period (mitcad#1532).

The roof slab rounded on all its edges with 0.66 to 0.86: the eave's end
edge's contacts are cut to the same two points by the corner at the tip (a
torus, PerformThreeCorner) and the plate at the obtuse end (1654), and
dropStripesCutToNothing (1640) drops its blend, the torus taking the
plate's curve with a p-curve of its own projected on the torus
(GeomProjLib). The projection landed a period away in u: the torus's face
was built over the other part of the torus, with an edge of no length that
is no degenerated edge (area -2.68 at r = 0.8).

- dropStripesCutToNothing: on a periodic surface the new p-curve is moved
  by whole periods to the start of the p-curve it replaces.

